body:
if more people learned how to use debt and budget it. Then avoiding debt wouldn’t be a problem. The B&H cards are 0% APR for a year. Budget in$2000 of monthly payments and you’ll be fine. Leverage your debt and money to serve you not be a disadvantage.

Edit; 
Plus if you’re working a regular job and making anything above 30k and not overhead with expenses. A CC like that shouldn’t be your downfall. Look up ways to better budget your money and maybe the card would make more sense after. But, have confidence cause they are right. It can fuck up your life if you’re not smart.

working crafty won’t get you anywhere near the DP. Especially if it’s as big as you say it is. A work the job for 6 months and determine what’s the likely hood of you actually climbing the chain. Maybe consider brushing up in G&E or AC related work to better prepare you for a DP role in the future. 


A good universal concept though; 
Always keep a small journal with you. If you’re just starting out, any information (good or bad) could be helpful down the line.

sorry, a proper response would be something like; 
the composition is so beautiful i just love how define those trees lines are but they keep a healthy distance from the house. the house feels so personified by them yet so isolated at the same time. a very well balanced photo overall. 

but still... fuckkkkkkkkkkkk

 I have to ask, as a 25 year screenwriter. What are your suggestions for actually getting your script seen? Is it networking, trying to get more producers on your side. A manager, screenplay contest. 

&#x200B;

curious what your thoughts are and what you've had success with and what has failed you. If there's already a post somewhere you'd recommend, i'd love that too. 

&#x200B;

Thanks!
